18. The Petitioner claims that its members such as employees at Moi Teaching and Referral Hospital,
Kenyatta National Hospital, public universities, public educational institutions, Kenya Power and
Lighting Company Ltd, domestic workers and allied workers do not fall within the category of public
ocers nor state ocers as envisaged by the Constitution.
19. The starting point in addressing the above issue would be the denition of public ocer under Article
260 of the Constitution which provides that a 'public ocer' is;
“(a) Any state ocer; or
(b) any person, other than a state ocer who holds a public oce”.
20. I am clear in my mind that the members of the Petitioner cannot be state ocers and the denition
of State ocers Under Article 260 of the Constitution bears me out because under that Article, 'state
oce' is dened thus;
“State oce” means any of the following oces—
