(p) Inspector-General, and the Deputy Inspectors-General, of Inspector-General, and the Deputy
Inspectors-General, of the National Police Service; or
(q) an oce established and designated as a State oce by national legislation;
9. A “State Ocer” is then dened by the same Article as a person holding any of the above oce. One
such person is “Member of Parliament” and “Member of a County Assembly”.
10. The above denitions are reproduced at Section 2 of the Leadership and Integrity Act, 2012 which
is “an Act of Parliament to give eect to,and establish procedures and mechanisms for the eective
administration of Chapter Six of the Constitution and connected purposes”. Article 77 is one of the
provisions within Chapter six of the Constitution and any reference to “State ocers” in it must
necessarily refer to the meaning assigned to the term by article 260 of the Constitution.
That article provides as follows;
(1) ) A full-time State ocer shall not participate in any other gainful employment.
